  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656222",
      "title": "How many Instances of Service Should It Be?",
      "lectureOrder": 435,
      "videoOrder": 399,
      "sourceHash": "1114ad41f1739b3238bb62a435bd3a886a6639e6371b2c972da30b5611998d66",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 3,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "we learned about that hierarchical injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 9.24,
          "en": "And actually, this injection behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.24,
          "end": 11.46,
          "en": "leads to the behavior we see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.46,
          "end": 13.77,
          "en": "Now, that's not a bug, that's intended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.77,
          "end": 16.62,
          "en": "You might have an application where you want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.62,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "many different instances of the same service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 23.19,
          "en": "where you absolutely don't want to have the same instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.19,
          "end": 25.65,
          "en": "But sometimes you want to have the same instance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "and we definitely do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 30.69,
          "en": "Because right now for our AccountsService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 32.55,
          "en": "we have three instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.55,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "The first one gets created here in AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 37.35,
          "en": "we provide it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.35,
          "end": 39.36,
          "en": "AppComponent receives its own service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.36,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "or its own instance of the service, I should say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 44.16,
          "en": "as to all the child components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.16,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "Now you might say, \"Fine,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "because new-account and account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "are child components, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "But there we provide it again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "and hence we override the instance we would get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 55.23,
          "en": "from the AppComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.23,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "Now, new-account and account.component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 59.97,
          "en": "have their own instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.97,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "So these are the other two instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "of this service class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 66.6,
          "en": "And therefore if we add a new service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 66.6,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "we call addAccount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "There we push it on this array of accounts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 70.59,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "and this actually works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 74.744,
          "en": "but it's a totally different instance of the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 74.744,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "than the one we use here in AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 79.23,
          "en": "the one through which we loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 79.23,
          "end": 81.72,
          "en": "How can we fix it then here for our app?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 85.59,
          "en": "Simple, we just remove it from the providers array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 85.59,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "Don't remove it from the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "We of course do need it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 90.9,
          "en": "because that tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 90.9,
          "end": 92.4,
          "en": "that we want an instance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 92.4,
          "end": 95.19,
          "en": "the providers array basically tells which instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 95.19,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "so there we needed to remove it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "And the same for account.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 100.62,
          "en": "leave it in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 100.62,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "leave the import at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 104.72999999999999,
          "en": "but remove it from the providers array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 104.72999999999999,
          "end": 106.14,
          "en": "With that little change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 106.14,
          "end": 108.843,
          "en": "if you go back to the application after saving it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 111.93,
          "en": "let's add another account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 111.93,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "Now you see it at the bottom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 116.61,
          "en": "now you can change the status again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 116.61,
          "end": 118.44,
          "en": "So this is the difference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 118.44,
          "end": 121.56,
          "en": "different instances of the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 121.56,
          "end": 124.98,
          "en": "Now we're using one of the same before we weren't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 127.44,
          "en": "Both may be the behavior you want in your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 130.083,
          "en": "but make sure that you get the correct one.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
